    "sources": {
      "rates": "City Power 'Schedule of Approved Tariffs for FY26/27' (8 pp, dated 01 July 2026). The source PDF is stored alongside this file as 2027-COJ.pdf (sha256 82ae90273dd458a8cf6aad6f5d806641789c3c0d0bf24cf5bcd12ba42301697a), so every rate here can be checked against the document it was transcribed from.",
      "rules": "CoJ Council Annexure 4, 'Amendment of Tariff of Charges for Electricity Services 1 July 2025 - 30 June 2026' (electricity pp. 40-53 of the 259-page CoJ budget document, PDF dated June 2025). Rules are FY25/26 text and are ASSUMED unchanged for FY26/27 unless the FY26/27 schedule says otherwise. The 259-page file contains no FY26/27 tariffs."
    },
    "units": {
      "energy_rate": "cents per kWh (c/kWh), excl. VAT",
      "service_and_capacity_charges": "Rand per month (R/month), excl. VAT",
      "demand_charge": "Rand per kVA (R/kVA), excl. VAT",
      "reactive_energy_charge": "cents per kVArh (c/kVArh), excl. VAT"
    },
    "schema_notes": [
      "energy_charges is a flat list of rate rows. season: all|summer|winter. period: all|peak|standard|off_peak. block/up_to_kwh are null for non-block rows.",
      "Block tariffs: up_to_kwh is the inclusive upper bound of the block (null = unbounded). Blocks are consecutive. Thresholds are per calendar month (confirmed: FY25/26 table header 'Consumption block kWh/month').",
      "null in fixed_charges / demand_charges / reactive_energy_charge means the source lists no such charge for that tariff.",
      "capacity_charge_r_per_month is what the FY25/26 annexure calls the 'Network charge'. Same charge, renamed in the FY26/27 schedule (60A single-phase R694.58 appears under both names).",
      "Season month ranges are in the top-level 'seasons' object.",
      "Calculation rules that a rate row alone does not capture (reactive energy, minimum demand, surcharges, prepaid reset, reseller treatment) are in 'billing_rules' and 'surcharges'. Do not compute reactive or demand charges from the rate fields alone."
    ],
    "source_corrections": [
      "'>500Wh' in the source (Prepaid Low/High, Reseller Conventional) read as '>500kWh'.",
      "Weekday off-peak printed as '12h00-06h00'; interpreted as 22h00-06h00 (only reading that covers the 24h day without overlap).",
      "Saturday/public-holiday standard period printed as '18h00-20h0'; interpreted as 18h00-20h00.",
      "Both TOU typos are also in the FY25/26 council annexure (5.4.7), so they are errors in the source, not transcription errors. The interpretations above are still inferences."
    ],
    "data_flags": [
      "Cross-check vs FY25/26 annexure (electricity, incl. TOU tariffs): 100 of 105 comparable rates rose by 9.0% (+/-0.15%), which corroborates the transcription. Reactive energy rose 9.0% (42.43 -> 46.25 c/kVArh). Exceptions: Prepaid Low block 3 (+11.5%), Prepaid High capacity charge (R130 -> R140, +7.7%), Prepaid High service charge (unchanged R70), Single Phase 60A service and capacity charges (both unchanged from FY25/26). Stored as printed in the FY26/27 schedule; may be deliberate policy.",
      "Industrial LV (TOU) demand charge R461.28/kVA vs R461.22 for non-TOU LV is correct: FY25/26 was R423.15 (TOU) vs R423.10 (non-TOU), and both scale by 9.0%.",
      "Embedded generator rates are exactly +15.0% on the FY25/26 annexure values (108.35 and 89.79). The FY25/26 budget schedule elsewhere in the same document shows slightly different values (108.67 and 90.05); FY26/27 matches the annexure figures.",
      "FY25/26 prepaid rule 1.7.17 says customers 'buy the initial 500 kWh in the month at the first block tariff', which conflicts with the 0-350 / 351-500 / >500 prepaid block tables in both years. Data follows the tables.",
      "FY25/26 also had an Industrial HV (TOU) tariff, a 'Robot Intersections' rate (R491.72) and a 'Streetlights & Billboard' rate (R551.23). None appear in the FY26/27 schedule, so they are not in this file."
    ]
